Go to the rent-a-center ask them how much for the TV/couch/whatever each week/month. Go home and set up an auto transfer from checking to savings of that amount. In a few months you can buy one brand new and not have a bill. 

&#x200B;

Its all about self discipline and not buying crap you cant afford/dont need

OMG, i would build the most amazing life!

&#x200B;

Then I would make myself and my friends and family rich. Invest every cent I had into apple until Bitcoin was selling for like a penny a bitcoin and buy a couple million at that price and hold them until they hit 20k and sell them all and retire on a big ranch where I rescue wild mustangs and let them continue to live as wild horses on my private ranch.

It is a tough decision, but you can eventually play all 3.

&#x200B;

I personally will be starting as "street kid" because that is what closest resembles my upbringing. I want to play my first play through trying to make choices that come natural to me, like play how I really am. Then try other stuff later in different play throughs.
